==English==

[[Image:Zamek-niepolomice.jpg|thumb|right|Courtyard of Castle of Polish Kings in Niepołomice, 25 km from Kraków (Cracow).]]

===Pronunciation===
{{wikipedia}}
* {{audio|en-us-courtyard.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈkoːt.jaːd/}}

===Etymology===
[[court]] + [[yard]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# an [[area]], [[open]] to the [[sky]], partially or wholly [[surrounded]] by [[wall]]s or [[building]]s
#: ''She sat in the '''courtyard''', enjoying the garden.''

